Item 7: stats.freed counted before vms.open() can fail (Marcelo)

Uncommitted on top of b1f6bbb71072 (series head, pushed); item7.diff = `git diff`.

FINDING
free_backing() (pools.rs, extracted in item 3 from reclaim_check()) adds the dropped chunks to
stats.freed before vms.open(). If the walk fails, the VMs' aliases still hold the pages: the
stat (and the info log's "N chunks freed") overstate what was freed.

VALIDATION OF THE FINDING: real, test-first.
New harness case failed_vm_walk_counts_nothing_freed (1500 posted, the idle reclaim at 1 s with
the registry walk failing once, FAIL_OPEN): on the unfixed code "FAILED. 36 passed; 1 failed":
"freed counted with the VM walk failed" (M3 ~/Projects/build-out/kernel-stack177/i7pre/).

FIX (pools.rs free_backing())
The dropped chunk count is added to stats.freed and returned only if the VMs were walked and
their aliases above keep_chunks() unmapped; on a failed walk it warns as before and returns 0,
so the info line says "0 chunks freed, 2 backed". The doc says why. The ledger and the chunk
list still drop the chunks (as before): every VM drops its stale aliases at its next
publication (VmState::map_heap()), which is when the pages go.
Harness: the case checks freed 0, the warning, the info line " 0 chunks freed", no Free event,
A still holding all its aliases; then A's next publication frees chunks-2 objects and leaves
2 aliases. Mutation freed-without-walk (returns `dropped` on the failure path) is caught by it.
Docstring bullet.

FIX VALIDATION (M3 chroot, ~/Projects/build-out/kernel-stack177/i7/)
